course: dictionary
lesson: 16127
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. To know which one is right, read the words around it, which is its context. «The leaf spun round and round in the whirlpool.» The clues are spun round and water, so a whirlpool is a place where water spins very fast.
explain: «Ben pulled the plug, and a tiny whirlpool swirled down the drain.» Here the clues are pulled the plug and drain, so this whirlpool is a small swirl in a bath. Try your meaning in the sentence to check it: water that spins round and pulls things down fits both sentences.
explain: The second meaning is about a bath. «Mum relaxed in the whirlpool bath after work.» A whirlpool bath is a bath where warm water swirls around, so the word fits the bath as well as the sea.
fact: A whirlpool is water that spins round and round very fast.
fact: «Whirlpool» can mean a place in a river or the sea that can pull things down into it.
fact: Whirlpools form where currents meet, where tides rush through narrow channels, or where water flows round rocks.
fact: The Corryvreckan, off the coast of Scotland, is a famous sea whirlpool.
fact: In water safety, you learn to stay away from whirlpools and fast water.
exercise: «The leaf spun round and round in the whirlpool.» What is a whirlpool? | *A place where water spins round and round very fast | A kind of warm bread | A tall rock on the shore | A small brown bird
exercise: «Ben pulled the plug, and a tiny whirlpool swirled down the drain.» What made the tiny whirlpool? | A ball of paper | Wind blowing through the window | *Water draining away from the bath | A cat jumped in the bath
exercise: Ella says a whirlpool can only be in a river. What is true? | *In the sea, in a river, or in a bath | Only in baths | Only in the sky | Only in rivers
test: «The sailors steered away from the whirlpool.» Why did they steer away? | They wanted a swim | They were lost in the fog | *It could pull their boat down into the water | The sea was too calm
test: Which word best means water that spins fast and pulls things down? | Splash | Ripple | Puddle | *Whirlpool
exam: What does whirlpool mean in «The swirling whirlpool sucked the stick under the water.»? | *A spot where water spins fast and pulls things down | A kind of warm drink | A dry hole in the ground | A tall wave on a beach
